WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.850
Two bromoalkanes share
the same formula: C₄H₉Br.

2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:09.990
Warm each one with hydroxide
ions, and both give an alcohol.

3
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:13.630
Same formula, same reagent,
same kind of product.

4
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.630
Yet they get there by
completely different routes.

5
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.030
Why do they swap bromine
for OH by different routes?

6
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:24.290
In this mission, you'll meet
the SN2 and SN1 mechanisms:

7
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:29.610
one step and two, with curly arrows, a
transition state and an intermediate.

8
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:33.570
You'll see a molecule turned inside
out, compare energy profiles,

9
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:37.170
and find out why
iodoalkanes react fastest.

10
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.950
Your mission: explain why the two
bromoalkanes react by different routes.
